My personal nvim settings

* Clone to ~/.config/nvim
* Symlink tmux.conf to ~/.tmux.conf
* Put openai key in ~/.config/openai.token

## Elixir (coc.nvim)

1. `:CocInstall coc-elixir`
2. The elixir-ls build bundled with coc-elixir is precompiled for an older
   Erlang/OTP and may crash on start ("please re-compile this module with an
   Erlang/OTP ... compiler"). If so, build ElixirLS's self-installing
   launcher from source instead (it rebuilds itself against whatever
   Elixir/OTP each project uses, so it won't need re-doing on upgrades):

   ```
   git clone https://github.com/elixir-lsp/elixir-ls.git /tmp/elixir-ls
   cd /tmp/elixir-ls
   mix local.hex --force --if-missing
   mix local.rebar --force --if-missing
   MIX_ENV=prod mix deps.get
   MIX_ENV=prod mix compile
   MIX_ENV=prod mix elixir_ls.release2 -o ~/.local/share/elixir-ls
   ```

3. Point coc-elixir at it via a machine-local `coc-settings.json` (ignored by
   git) in this directory:

   ```json
   {
     "elixir.pathToElixirLS": "/home/<you>/.local/share/elixir-ls/language_server.sh"
   }
   ```


